From: Boxedwine project
Subject: [PATCH] ddraw: Accumulate legacy screen extents for vertex draws.

Force Commander uses SetClipStatus / GetClipStatus to measure rendered unit
bounds for mouse picking. Returning the whole viewport makes empty ground
above units select those units and prevents move orders.

Track XYZ extents for immediate, strided and vertex-buffer draws, and XYZRHW
extents for immediate draws, including indexed variants. Match native
projection, viewport clipping, per-draw
padding, reset and accumulation behavior. Keep the existing conservative
fallback for unsupported vertex blending. Clipping-status bit calculation
and ProcessVertices / execute-buffer extent operations remain outside scope.

Native Windows and Boxedwine regression: tools/buildWine/probes/d3d7-extents.c
Gameplay: Force Commander demo upward movement confirmed with original game.

---
--- a/dlls/ddraw/ddraw_private.h
+++ b/dlls/ddraw/ddraw_private.h
@@ -368,6 +368,9 @@
 
     /* For temporary saving state during reset. */
     struct wined3d_stateblock *saved_state;
